    "South should duck the first round of diamonds in the dummy. The defense will win cheaply, but the contract will be secure as long as diamonds are 3-2.",
    "South must be careful to win a club return in the closed hand, preserving the ♣K for a late dummy entry. A diamond is now played to the ♦K or ♦Q. South will not only make his contract (when diamonds are 3-2), but 2 overtricks as well. The recommended line of play will also succeed if either defender was dealt a singleton ♦A."
